<title>USA: Loctite insiders to delay tender of some shares.</title>
<headline>Loctite insiders to delay tender of some shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loctite Corp said that some of its directors and officers told the company they would withhold some of their holdings in the first phase of Henkel KGaA's tender offer.</p>
<p>Loctite said about 84,000 shares in total, or about 0.26 percent of those outstanding, were being withheld for tax-planning purposes. It said the executives plan to tender the shares in the second stage of the merger.</p>
<p>The company also said it continued to recommend that shareholders tender their shares pursuant to the offer.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
